          %hr/
          .standout
            %p
              All of the following assumes that the reader is well familiar with the basic ideas indicated at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
          %p
            In the following
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mi RB
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d-RB
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Bord_d
            and the like denotes a category of
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+cobordism"} Riemannian cobordism
            = succeed "," do
              %em Riemannian structure
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mi E
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d-E B
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E Bord_d
            or the like denotes a category of cobordisms with
            = succeed "," do
              %em Euclidean structure
            %em flat
            Riemannian metric.
          %p The definition of this is discussed in detail in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+categories+following+Stolz-Teichner"} bordism categories following Stolz-Teichner
          %p
            %strong definition
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            \-dimensional Riemannian field theories are symmetric monoidal functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mi RB
                  %mo →
                  %mi TV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d-RB \to TV
            from
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
          %p
            A field theory is very similar to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            of a group. Only where a representation of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a functor from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G = {*}//G
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            is a representation of a more complicated domain category.
          %p
            %strong
              how does
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
              enter?
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            there is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mi RB
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d-RB(X)
          %p
            of Riemannian bordisms equipped with a continuous map to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Notice that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi RB
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d RB(X)
            does depend covariantly on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Fun
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi RB
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi TV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun^\otimes(d RB(X), TV)
            is contravariant in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p When special structure is around, however, we also have a push-forward of such functors along morphisms.
          %p
            %strong> Example: push-forward to the point
            \: for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as above and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to {*}
            the unique map to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            heuristically we want a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi RFT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                  %mi d
                  %mi RFT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi pt
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d RFT(X) \stackrel{p_*}{\to} d RFT(pt)
          %p
            notice that this push-forward is not an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theories
          %p heuristically the pushforward
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi RFT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                  %mi d
                  %mi RFT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi pt
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d RFT(X) \stackrel{p_*}{\to} d RFT(pt)
          %p
            acts on field theories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_X
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_X \mapsto E
          %p by the assignment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Γ
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Maps
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi regarded
                    %mi as
                    %mi a
                    %mi vector
                    %mi bundle
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E(Y^{d-1}) \mapsto
                  \\Gamma\left(
                  \\array{
                  E_X(Y)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  Maps(Y,X)
                  }
                  regarded as a vector bundle
                  \\right)
          %p
            for instance when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_X(Y) = \mathbb{C}
            then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(Y) = \Gamma(Maps(Y,X))
          %p
            For instance take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            to be the pair of pants with input
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_0
            and output
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_1
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \Sigma \to X
            be a map.
          %p
            Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\Sigma)
            will take some section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi \in E(Y_0)
            to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Z
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi dvol
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E(\Sigma)(\Psi) : (f_1 : Y_1 \to X)
                  \\mapsto
                  \\int_{\{F : \Sigma \to X\} | F/Y_1 = f_1} E_X(F)(\Psi(f_0))
                  \\frac{1}{Z}\exp(-S(F) dvol)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here the expression
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mi Z
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi dvol
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{Z}\exp(-S(F) dvol)
            denotes a would-be measure which is still to be defined.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0 = F/Y_0
            is the restriction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_0
          %p
            Contravariant functors with push-forward also arise as part of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Diff
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h^n : Diff^{op} \to Ab
          %p
            from the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            of smooth
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            of abelian groups that satisfies the axioms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theory.
          %p These Eilenberg-Steenrod axioms are
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %strong homotopy axiom
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^n
            %li
              %p
                %strong Mayer-Vietoris axiom
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^n
            %li
              %p
                %strong suspension isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msubsup
                        %mi h
                        %mi cvs
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^n(X) \simeq h^{n+1}_{cvs}(X \times \mathbb{R})
          %p
            here in the last axiom for
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^{n+1}(\Sigma X)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi cvs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_{cvs}
            means “compact vertical support”.
          %p
            Concerning the
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong homotopy axiom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            that sends manifolds to a category of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mi FTs
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Diff
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d-FTs := h : Diff^{op} \to C
          %p
            in
            = succeed "s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dRFT
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dRFT
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_0, \omega_1 \in h(X)
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordance"} concordant
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists \omega \in h(X \times \mathbb{R})
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega/(X\times \{i\}) \simeq \omega_i
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 0,1
          %p then under this relation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mi RFT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \mapsto  d-RFT(X)/\simeq
          %p is a homotopy invariant functor
          %p
            %strong> Homework
            \: for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi closed
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(X) = \Omega^n_{closed}(X)
          %p
            we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_0
            concordant to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            exactly when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi d
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_0 = \omega_1 + d \alpha
            for some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \Omega^{n-1}(X)
          %p
            Concerning the
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong Mayer-Vietoris axiom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = U \cup V
            then the functor should respect this gluing.
          %p
            suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %mi RFT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in 2-RFT(X)
            is a 2d Riemmanian field theory. let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma : S^1 \to X
            be a loop in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\gamma)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            sits neither entirely in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            or in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(\gamma)
            can be reconstructed by knowing just the restriction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            So this is a
            %strong problem
            for the definition of field theories so far.
          %p
            The
            %strong proposed solution
            (from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/What+is+an+elliptic+object%3F"} What is an elliptic object?
            %em extended
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            %strong locality
            into
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-category"} n-categories
          %p This will however not be studied here for the moment.
          %p
            Concerning the
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong suspension isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
            the notion of a field theory over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi RFTs
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \mapsto d-RFTs^n(X)
          %p
            such that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=0
            this is an ordinary Riemannian field theory, in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mi RFT
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d-RFT(X)
          %p
            This requires to replace
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
          %p
            %strong Example
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 0
            and consider 0-dimensional TFTs over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p so consider
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Fun
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Bord
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi TV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Fun^\otimes(0 Bord(X), TV)
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Bord
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 Bord(X)
            there is only a single
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
            which has a unique map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \to X
          %p
            the collecton of morphisms is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi finite
                  %mi set
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{finite set \to X\}
            in there is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi pt
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{Diff}(pt,X)
          %p here composition of morphisms is the same as tensor product of objects: both comes from the disjoint union of these finite set domains.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo :
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Bord
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi TV
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E : 0 Bord(X) \to TV_{\mathbb{R}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\emptyset \mapsto \mathbb{R}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} mathb
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x \in X \mapsto E(X) \in \mathb{R}
          %p so a priori we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Fun
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Bord
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi TV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Fun^\otimes(0 Bord(X), TV) \simeq Maps(X, \mathbb{R})
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right we have
            %em all
            maps.
          %p
            This is not quite what is intended. We want to see
            %em smooth
            maps on the right. To get that, we need to talk about
            %em smooth functors
            on the left. This is the topic of later discussion, which will yield
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SmoothFun
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Bord
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi TV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SmoothFun^\otimes(0 Bord(X), TV) \simeq C^\infty(X, \mathbb{R})
                  \\,.
          %p
            But one other ting goes wrong the: the corresponding homotopy functor is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)/\simeq = \{0\}
          %p
            The way out to that will be to go to
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
          %p
            %strong Punchline
            of this session here:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %mi TFTs
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi SmoothFun
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Bord
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi TV
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (0|1)-TFTs(X)
                  \\simeq
                  SmoothFun^\otimes((0|1)Bord(X), TV)
          %p
            and then it is a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi lemma
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lemma^G
            that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SuperDiff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C^\infty(SuperDiff(\mathbb{R}^{0|1}, X))^G
                  \\simeq
                  \\Omega^\bullet(X)^G
                  \= (\oplus_{n = 0}^{\infty} \Omega^n(X))^G
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} wim
                    %mn 42
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⋊
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = Diff(\mathbb{R}^{0|1}) \wim42 \mathbb{R}^{0|1} \rtimes \mathbb{R}^\times
          %p
            The degree decomposition on forms then turns out to be the eigenvalue decompositon of the
            = succeed "-part," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\times
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0|1}
          %p
            so then from that one finds that the
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %em closed
            0-forms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi closed
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(X)^G
                  \\simeq
                  \\Omega^0_{closed}(X)
          %p
            So we get
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %strong Lemma
            \:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi TFT
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (0|1)-TFT^n(X) \simeq \Omega^n_{cl}(X)
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mi TFT
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi concord
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (0|1)-TFT^n(X)_{concord} \simeq H^n_{dR}(X)
          %p
            %strong push-forward
          %p Now with the super-directions included, there is a notion of push-forward of the TFTs that does shift the degree, and we get the following
          %p
            %strong Theorem (Stolz-Teichner-Kreck-Hohnhold)
          %p
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is oriented
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi TFT
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi push
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi TFT
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (0|1)TFT^n(X) \stackrel{push}{\to} (0|1)TFT^0
                  \\simeq \mathbb{R}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi n
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi pt
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^n_{cl}(X) \stackrel{\int_{X_n}}{\to}
                  \\Omega^0_{cl}(pt)
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathbb{R}
          %p
            and similarly after dividing out concordance, the push-forward becomes the push-forward in
